   "name": "C10-education",
   "turns": [
    {
     "replyText": "Pearls are delicate and benefit from gentle care. Here's how to keep them beautiful:Regular cleaning: Wipe pearls with a soft, damp cloth after wearing them to remove oils and sweat. Use lukewarm water and dry them thoroughly with a soft cloth.Deeper cleaning: For a more thorough clean, use a soft cloth dampened with lukewarm water and a drop of mild soap. Gently wipe each pearl, then rinse with a clean, damp cloth and dry completely.What to avoid: Never use harsh chemicals, ultrasonic cleaners, or steam cleaners on pearls—they can damage the delicate nacre (the lustrous outer layer). Don't soak pearls for extended periods or expose them to extreme temperatures.Storage: Keep pearls in a soft pouch or lined jewelry box, separate from harder stones that might scratch them. Store them away from direct sunlight and extreme heat or humidity.The key is gentle handling and keeping them clean and dry. Proper care will help your pearls maintain their luster for years.",
